# Production deployment rules

Before public launch ensure:
- only intended public ports/services exposed;
- PostgreSQL/Redis/private services isolated from Internet;
- TLS, HSTS, CSP and other security headers configured;
- WAF/DDoS/bot controls at ingress (for example Cloudflare) plus server-side controls;
- SSH/management uses keys, no password/root login where avoidable, and preferably private management network/VPN;
- production containers run with least privilege and minimal images;
- secrets can be rotated without code changes;
- database backups + restore procedure are documented/tested;
- monitoring/alerts exist for uptime, 5xx, auth abuse, payment/provider failures, unusual AI burn, DB/queue health;
- dependency/security update process exists;
- emergency switches exist for expensive AI capabilities;
- admin/control plane receives stronger ingress/auth controls than consumer app.
